WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.055 --> 00:00:06.276
Once again Scrooge felt himself swallowed up in the darkness of the spirit's cloak.

2
00:00:06.277 --> 00:00:15.008
He emerged a moment later into daylight, in a room occupied by a young mother and a few children.

3
00:00:15.009 --> 00:00:20.257
The mother paced the room, stopping now and then to peer out the window.

4
00:00:20.258 --> 00:00:27.572
Finally the door opened and a young man came in, stomping the snow off his boots.

5
00:00:27.573 --> 00:00:32.519
"Is it good news or bad?" the woman asked anxiously.

6
00:00:32.520 --> 00:00:38.379
"I think it's mostly bad news," the man said.

7
00:00:38.380 --> 00:00:43.459
"We still don't have enough money to pay off our whole debt."

8
00:00:43.460 --> 00:00:48.294
"Oh, no." She collapsed into a chair.

9
00:00:48.295 --> 00:00:54.208
"Wait! There is still hope, Caroline," her husband said.

10
00:00:54.209 --> 00:00:59.779
"I just learned something—he is dead."

11
00:00:59.780 --> 00:01:04.273
The woman gasped. "He's dead?

12
00:01:04.274 --> 00:01:07.729
But that means our debt will be transferred to someone else.

13
00:01:07.730 --> 00:01:10.955
Who will we owe money to now?"

14
00:01:10.956 --> 00:01:14.497
"I don't know," her husband said.

15
00:01:14.498 --> 00:01:19.756
"But at least we have more time to gather the money we owe.

16
00:01:19.757 --> 00:01:25.157
And I doubt anyone could be as heartless as Ebenezer Scrooge was.

17
00:01:25.158 --> 00:01:31.466
So, perhaps we can sleep tonight with lighter hearts."

18
00:01:31.467 --> 00:01:39.349
Scrooge scowled. "This isn't fair, spirit! I barely know these people.

19
00:01:39.350 --> 00:01:43.873
Show me someone whose opinion I know better—and respect."

20
00:01:43.874 --> 00:01:47.482
As usual, the ghost said nothing.

21
00:01:47.483 --> 00:01:55.796
It only flung its cloak wide, sweeping away the room and returning Scrooge to the busy streets of London.

22
00:01:55.797 --> 00:02:03.130
Then it pointed its bony hand at two well-dressed gentlemen talking on a busy corner.

23
00:02:03.131 --> 00:02:08.007
"I know those two men very well," Scrooge said with a nod.

24
00:02:08.008 --> 00:02:14.220
"Like the others we saw earlier, they're wealthy and important businessmen.

25
00:02:14.221 --> 00:02:18.464
And I always made a point of treating them fairly in business.

26
00:02:18.465 --> 00:02:22.845
I'm sure they respect me a great deal for that."

27
00:02:22.846 --> 00:02:26.928
Scrooge moved closer to his acquaintances.

28
00:02:26.929 --> 00:02:30.881
"How are you?" one businessman said to the other.

29
00:02:30.882 --> 00:02:36.127
"I'm very well, and how are you?" the second man said.

30
00:02:36.128 --> 00:02:41.297
"Did you hear that old Ebenezer Scrooge has died?"

31
00:02:41.298 --> 00:02:44.541
"Yes, I heard something about that."

32
00:02:44.542 --> 00:02:49.020
The first man wrapped his scarf more tightly around his neck.

33
00:02:49.021 --> 00:02:53.011
"Brr. It's quite cold today, isn't it?"

34
00:02:53.012 --> 00:02:59.515
"The weather is right for Christmastime, though, I suppose," the second man said.

35
00:02:59.516 --> 00:03:03.410
"Do you like to ice skate?"

36
00:03:03.411 --> 00:03:09.266
"No." The first man chuckled. "My oldest son enjoys it, though.

37
00:03:09.267 --> 00:03:14.433
He'll be so happy about this weather. Good morning!"

38
00:03:14.434 --> 00:03:18.084
With a tip of their hats, the two men parted ways.

39
00:03:18.085 --> 00:03:22.841
Scrooge glared after them as they disappeared.

40
00:03:22.842 --> 00:03:28.728
"We did so much business together, and that's all they have to say about my death?

41
00:03:28.729 --> 00:03:34.212
Why, the cold weather was more interesting to them than the news of my passing."

42
00:03:34.213 --> 00:03:36.890
The spirit didn't move.

43
00:03:36.891 --> 00:03:41.359
"Show me something else, spirit!" Scrooge demanded angrily.

44
00:03:41.360 --> 00:03:46.121
"This time I want to see some truly sad feelings about death."

45
00:03:46.122 --> 00:03:53.008
Whoosh! The ghost swept his black cloak, gathering Scrooge into darkness.

46
00:03:53.009 --> 00:03:58.299
When Scrooge could see again, he found himself back in Bob Cratchit's house.

47
00:03:58.300 --> 00:04:02.267
"That's more like it," Scrooge said.

48
00:04:02.268 --> 00:04:07.293
"My clerk and his family will be very sad to learn of my passing.

49
00:04:07.294 --> 00:04:13.669
If nothing else, it means his paycheck will stop until he finds other employment."

50
00:04:13.670 --> 00:04:18.597
The Cratchit home was much quieter than the last time Scrooge had seen it.

51
00:04:18.598 --> 00:04:24.101
Bob Cratchit was nowhere to be seen, and neither was his daughter Martha.

52
00:04:24.102 --> 00:04:28.516
Mrs. Cratchit and Belinda were sewing by the light of the fire.

53
00:04:28.517 --> 00:04:34.680
Sam and Sarah were listening to Peter, who was reading quietly from the family's bible.

54
00:04:34.681 --> 00:04:41.319
"'And He took a child, and set him in the midst of them,'" Peter read.

55
00:04:41.320 --> 00:04:45.793
Mrs. Cratchit looked up and set her sewing down on a table.

56
00:04:45.794 --> 00:04:48.919
"Oh, please don't read any more, Peter.

57
00:04:48.920 --> 00:04:51.684
Especially not when your father gets home.

58
00:04:51.685 --> 00:04:55.894
It will only make poor Papa even sadder."

59
00:04:55.895 --> 00:05:00.140
"There, you see?" Scrooge smiled.

60
00:05:00.141 --> 00:05:04.282
"The whole family is upset that I'm dead!"

61
00:05:04.283 --> 00:05:09.977
The spirit stared at Scrooge for a moment before pointing back to the family.

62
00:05:09.978 --> 00:05:15.146
Scrooge watched Belinda jump to her feet and hug her mother.

63
00:05:15.147 --> 00:05:20.425
"Oh, Mother. We all miss him terribly. What will we do?"

64
00:05:20.426 --> 00:05:24.971
The other children ran over to throw their arms around the two of them.

65
00:05:24.972 --> 00:05:28.418
"It's not right, Mother," Sarah said with a sob.

66
00:05:28.419 --> 00:05:35.418
"Why did he have to die? Why did we have to lose our precious brother?"

67
00:05:35.419 --> 00:05:40.848
Scrooge gasped. The spirit was indeed showing him sadness about death.

68
00:05:40.849 --> 00:05:44.561
But the Cratchit family wasn't sad about Scrooge's death.

69
00:05:44.562 --> 00:05:53.922
They were mourning their beloved son and brother, Tiny Tim!

